{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And to Levi he said.</b> On account of Levi he said to HaShem, like \"say for me, he is my brother\":" "<b>Your devout man.</b> The man who is Your devout one:" "<b>Whom You tested at Massah.</b> The word is like בנסיון (in a test), and the meaning is that he was devout and no flaw was found in him except for the matter of Meribah, for which You already punished him. This too will support my interpretation regarding the matter of the calf, for he did it for the honor of HaShem:" "And the meaning of <b>Your Thummim and Your Urim.</b> That they shall always be his and his seed's:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:24.858018863Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}